# Proposed CODEOWNERS for the layout after step 3 of the separation plan.
#
# NOT ENABLED. GitHub reads .github/CODEOWNERS, and this file is not that. To enable
# it: copy these lines to .github/CODEOWNERS, replace the placeholder team names with
# real ones, and turn on "Require review from Code Owners" for main in the branch
# protection rules. A team name that does not exist makes GitHub ignore its line.
#
# The point is the contract. api/ is what the server and the interface agree on, so a
# change to it needs a person from each side. The rest follows who maintains it.

# The contract. Both sides review it.
/api/                      @Flockdeck/server-owners @Flockdeck/ui-owners

# The interface, and the files that keep it apart from the server.
/ui/                       @Flockdeck/ui-owners
/.github/boundary/         @Flockdeck/server-owners @Flockdeck/ui-owners

# The server. The relay registry and the access table are the two places where a new
# message or command is classified, so they are named.
/internal/                 @Flockdeck/server-owners
/internal/server/relayscrub.go    @Flockdeck/server-owners
/internal/server/viewerrole.go    @Flockdeck/server-owners
/main.go                   @Flockdeck/server-owners @Flockdeck/ui-owners
